@startuml
title UML sequence - partner consent, partner-drafted payment and revocation while the payment is in flight (AT-21)
actor "Security admin" as Admin
actor "Security approver" as Approver
participant "Partner app" as Partner
participant "Issuer (partners realm)" as Issuer
participant "bank-api" as API
participant "Identity functions" as I
participant "Controls" as C
participant "Payments" as P
actor Customer
participant "bank-worker" as W
Admin -> API : propose partner-budget (scopes, quota, loopback callback)
API -> I : partner_propose -> PENDING_APPROVAL (signing secret sealed, shown once)
Approver -> API : decision APPROVE (different person)
API -> I : partner_decide -> ACTIVE
Partner -> Issuer : client_credentials
Issuer --> Partner : 30 s token (aud bank-partner, azp partner-budget)
Partner -> API : POST /partner/v1/consents (version header, token)
API -> I : registry ACTIVE? quota? consent_request -> AWAITING_AUTHORIZATION
API --> Partner : consentId + bank authorization URL
Customer -> API : open #/connected/{id}; choose own accounts; allow
API -> I : consent_authorize -> ACTIVE; queue consent.authorized
W -> Partner : signed callback (HMAC t.body)
Partner -> API : quote + draft payment (Consent-Id)
API -> I : consent_binding -> partner actor (customer subject, PARTNER trust)
API -> P : create_intent (no challenge for partners)
P -> C : authorize -> identity.consent_permits(live)
Customer -> API : approve draft with action-bound step-up; confirm
API -> P : confirm -> ACCEPTED, authorized_actor = customer
Customer -> API : disconnect the app
API -> I : consent_revoke -> REVOKED; queue consent.revoked
Partner -> API : any consented call
API --> Partner : 403 (not distinguished)
W -> P : execute with the authorized customer actor
P --> W : SETTLED once; intent keeps partner as initiator
@enduml
